      "text": "Days 7–10: Maroon Culture in Upper Suriname"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "32e98cc56e915b24246f24ac4ba45ef7ec8c685c5b2821100b1eeea40adaecdf",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-46f95238a290459398b4283e1f15ccba",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "After Paramaribo, head inland again to Upper Suriname. Stay at a riverside lodge and learn about Maroon culture.\n\nMaroons are descendants of people who escaped slavery. Their villages and traditional ways of life have largely survived to this day. You’ll spend the nights in simple, clean riverside lodges.\n\nOn a walk through the village, you’ll see how residents go about their daily lives. Women from the village will perform traditional dances and invite guests to join in.\n\nThe programme also includes a walk through the jungle and a trip to river rapids where you can swim. After three days, return to Paramaribo and transfer to your hotel.\n\nMeals: breakfast, lunch and dinner."
    },
